# Factory-tree /etc/shadow, copied into the /etc subvol on first boot by
# tmpfiles C!; later passwd edits persist across image upgrades.
#
# root ships with the BOOTSTRAP password `changeme`. This is the only
# credential in the image: no interactive user is provisioned by default
# (myosi-homed-user@user.service is shipped DISABLED — the operator creates
# a real, properly-named user on first boot; see README "Post-installation").
#
# Why a known hash is acceptable here, and what bounds it:
#   - Console only. sshd is publickey-only (AuthenticationMethods publickey,
#     PasswordAuthentication no, PermitRootLogin prohibit-password), so this
#     password grants nothing remotely. Physical/console access is required.
#   - It is meant to be destroyed on first boot. The documented flow ends in
#     `passwd -l root`, after which no known credential remains.
#
# Override it for real fleets: bake your own hash over this file via
# mkosi.local.conf ExtraTrees=.
#
# Interactive users are owned by systemd-homed, not seeded here.
